	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["164F0808EF9DF557"]
			description: ["The lunar drill was a visitor; the &6EV Tripod Drill&r moves in, on titanium legs with a solar wing on each side. It is crafted from the old lunar drill, and titanium bits off an EV lathe: a full cycle can wear out one per bore. It only drills the veins of the Moon and Mars, and it is where all your titanium and tungsten come from. Let a lathe keep bits flowing by ME, and ship the ore home."]
			icon: "gtceu:ev_vein_drill"
			id: "5107982325BE34B7"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "7D0D9D1EEC42BBEB", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 8, id: "7C99B717F081DB18", item: "grindless:titanium_drill_bit", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ count: 16L, id: "31582C1C38CC314C", item: "grindless:titanium_drill_bit", type: "item" }
				{ count: 18L, id: "123430355F4FAED8", item: "grindless:solar_wing_panel", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1C53BF2915922005", item: "gtceu:ev_vein_drill", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "EV Tripod Drill"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5107982325BE34B7"]
			description: [
				"There's no water up here, so there's no drilling mud either, and a dry bit wears out fast. By day the solar wings cover half the bill; at night Earth pays all of it over the bridge."
				"Swap an output bus for an ME Output Bus and the ilmenite ships itself home."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:raw_ilmenite"
			id: "321540F2528D14FA"
			rewards: [{ id: "3C91B7DB655E3564", type: "xp", xp: 50 }]
			tasks: [{ count: 64L, id: "159814B37781817F", item: "gtceu:raw_ilmenite", type: "item" }]
			title: "Drilling Dry"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["33EFC07080657F50", "70F4075BAF69DA99"]
			description: ["The &6Regolith Cell&r cooks moon dirt until it gives up oxygen and metal, and it only works up here. A hall of sintered brick around a crucible ringed with nichrome coils, and a platinum electrode in the input bus as its anode. Circuit 1 releases solar wind gases, circuit 2 gives oxygen and iron, and on circuit 3 it bakes bricks faster than a furnace. Give each gas its own output hatch, or let one ME output hatch take the lot."]
			icon: "gtceu:regolith_cell"
			id: "5BEACE3F7A414F40"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "138B6A7977750137", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ id: "55ADFF45989716A6", item: "grindless:platinum_electrode", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "3955EAB8FBFF6100", item: "gtceu:regolith_cell", type: "item" }]
			title: "Regolith Cell"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5BEACE3F7A414F40"]
			description: [
				"On circuit 2 the cell melts regolith and runs current through it. Oxygen bubbles off the platinum anode, and iron and silicon settle out."
				"That oxygen fills your suit and feeds the cryogenic plant."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:oxygen_bucket"
			id: "320CD85A4C8D87D5"
			rewards: [{ id: "79FE3323A8B1B780", type: "xp", xp: 35 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "33B726E8B2DB7D96", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Oxygen from Rock"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["320CD85A4C8D87D5", "321540F2528D14FA"]
			description: [
				"Ilmenite dust in molten calcium chloride, current through it, and the oxygen leaves for the anode while the titanium stays behind. Same energy as the long way, and no chlorine at all."
				"It runs on circuit 2 with the &6Molten Salt Charge&r in the bus, and the charge never gets used up. The platinum plant has calcium chloride to spare."
			]
			icon: "grindless:molten_salt_charge"
			id: "33176DE8937B3BEE"
			rewards: [{ id: "125FC86C33CAA992", type: "xp", xp: 50 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1CB526CAE9B11C78", item: "grindless:molten_salt_charge", type: "item" }]
			title: "Titanium without Chlorine"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["14DF849D657D6AEF"]
			description: ["The &6Ore Refinery&r takes raw ore through the macerator, the washer, the thermal centrifuge and the sifter in a single recipe. Plain water for the washer, and a steady stream of raw ore. Many ores at once, with every byproduct in one place. Raw ore in from the drills by ME, dusts out to the lines."]
			icon: "gtceu:ore_refinery"
			id: "77E698504E2588EF"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "5D609A8EA5A94F14", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 8, id: "317F49D6060AD547", item: "gtceu:steel_plate", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "17CC74FF30958C80", item: "gtceu:ore_refinery", type: "item" }]
			title: "Ore Refinery"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77E698504E2588EF"]
			description: ["The &6Hot Strip Mill&r rolls a hot ingot straight into plates, rods or foil, skipping the freezer and the bender. A circuit that picks the shape, and cooling water that comes out as steam, so give it a turbine to go to. Faster metal for every line. Ingots that need liquid helium still go to the freezer. Ingots in by ME, plates and rods out, and the steam into the combined-cycle plant."]
			icon: "gtceu:hot_strip_mill"
			id: "7637A9813DB73D6B"
			rewards: [{ id: "352FB77A52EC3415", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "5BE8B5540509D143", item: "gtceu:hot_strip_mill", type: "item" }]
			title: "Hot Strip Mill"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7637A9813DB73D6B", "004525B795119B1B"]
			description: ["The platinum line is about forty recipes across a dozen machines; the &6Platinum Plant&r packs it into one hall, loops and all. Nitration mixture and ammonium chloride flowing first, and an electrode that wears out rarely: after the first one, made from End platinum, the plant pays for its own. Platinum, rhodium, ruthenium and palladium. Iridium and osmium from Earth's ore don't exist: those wait for Mercury. A battery buffer, plenty of output hatches and a place for every fluid."]
			icon: "gtceu:platinum_plant"
			id: "1F70EF41E5F8ED95"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "3EACE716001AFAEB", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ id: "1E92FF3E0CABF2CA", item: "grindless:platinum_electrode", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "593E46F6C0670998", item: "grindless:platinum_electrode", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1B3F08EE9C03B6B0", item: "gtceu:platinum_plant", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Platinum Plant"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5BEACE3F7A414F40"]
			description: ["The &6Cryogenic Plant&r liquefies gases at night for half the vacuum freezer's energy, and only runs on the Moon. A frostproof tower on sintered brick with a wing of &6Night-Sky Radiators&r on each side. Keep the radiators uncovered. Liquid nitrogen, liquid oxygen and the stockpile IV will ask for. Gas from the cell goes in by hatch, liquids go out to tanks."]
			icon: "gtceu:cryogenic_plant"
			id: "79EE0C54F2D89358"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "12ED220DB70AD3CF", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 2, id: "1E34767BB12D9536", item: "grindless:night_sky_radiator", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ count: 12L, id: "3F869B2BB13436B0", item: "grindless:night_sky_radiator", type: "item" }
				{ id: "58324638CAF43E78", item: "gtceu:cryogenic_plant", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Cryogenic Plant"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["79EE0C54F2D89358"]
			description: [
				"GregTech never liquefied nitrogen, but the cryogenic plant does. Check the tooltip of every pipe and tank it goes through, since not all of them like cryogenic fluids."
				"In the tripod's input hatch it keeps the bit cold: more ore, much less wear. Let the hatch run low and the tripod drills dry."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:liquid_nitrogen_bucket"
			id: "71F33D9D6D486DFE"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "3ECB34DDDF8FD7F8", type: "xp", xp: 45 }
				{ id: "3AA211C12A2B4DF1", item: "gtceu:stainless_steel_fluid_cell", type: "item" }
			]
			tasks: [{ id: "1BBB212BC73F2606", item: "gtceu:liquid_nitrogen_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Liquid Nitrogen"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["79EE0C54F2D89358"]
			description: [
				"The cell's oxygen becomes &6Liquid Oxygen&r here, as fast as in the freezer and at half the energy once the sun's down. The controller tells you what the next run will cost."
				"Start a stockpile of liquid oxygen and liquid helium: IV's extreme engines want the first, its hottest ingots the second."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:liquid_oxygen_bucket"
			id: "587829FDC7BAB863"
			rewards: [{ id: "147BF2D687A70D59", type: "xp", xp: 40 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7C844C0B7BCB595B", item: "gtceu:liquid_oxygen_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Liquid Oxygen"
			x: 8.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E510A95C066D14C"]
			description: ["No air, no fire. Bring a diesel generator up here and it'll just sit there, looking embarrassed. Methalox and rocket fuel carry their own oxygen; EMI lists where everything else burns."]
			icon: "minecraft:flint_and_steel"
			id: "16E2B1FFE70AC165"
			rewards: [{ id: "31B61BB841330806", type: "xp", xp: 20 }]
			shape: "circle"
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "36E0705B646B27B6", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Vacuum: Nothing Burns"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5BEACE3F7A414F40"]
			description: ["The &6Lunar Solar Array&r is rows of wing panels on titanium posts over sintered brick. With circuit 1 in its input bus, every panel that sees open sky pays out by day. Wing panels, a clear sky and brick footings. Moon power that needs no fuel. At night it rests, so buffers or Earth over the bridge keep the lights on. Wire it to a battery buffer and let the bridge fill the gap."]
			icon: "gtceu:lunar_solar_array"
			id: "734B97375A3121C4"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "75E155745FD05519", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 3, id: "1D1C45A97E81AA5B", item: "grindless:solar_wing_panel", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "32C9AF4491B411D4", item: "gtceu:lunar_solar_array", type: "item" }]
			title: "Lunar Solar Array"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["16E2B1FFE70AC165"]
			description: ["A gas turbine throws its exhaust away while it's still hot. The &6Combined-Cycle Plant&r sends it through a boiler instead, so the same fuel also spins a &6Large Steam Turbine&r. A large gas turbine controller and distilled water. It needs no rotor. More EU from the same fuel. If the steam has nowhere to go, the whole plant stops. Distilled water by pipe, fuel by ME, and make sure the output never backs up."]
			icon: "gtceu:combined_cycle_plant"
			id: "1DD071239194961D"
			rewards: [{ id: "1CD1FF02CF964051", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "39AE70B2671E0A18", item: "gtceu:combined_cycle_plant", type: "item" }
				{ id: "554E1B9CAF293B9A", item: "gtceu:steam_large_turbine", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Combined-Cycle Plant"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["734B97375A3121C4"]
			description: ["The &6Sealed Dome&r is a greenhouse that brings its own soil and makes a sky out of lamps. Water and carbon dioxide. Mars supplies the carbon dioxide from its air; up here it has to come from home. On circuit 5 (Moon) or 6 (Mars) it grows crops and breathes out oxygen. Water and gas by hatch, harvest by output bus."]
			icon: "gtceu:sealed_dome"
			id: "56820468F118D3EA"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "320FD462BCBA4081", type: "xp", xp: 60 }
				{ count: 9, id: "77DB74D40CF625D1", item: "minecraft:dirt", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "7D87303BAEF28490", item: "gtceu:sealed_dome", type: "item" }]
			title: "Sealed Dome"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["734B97375A3121C4", "5C4613715A82BDBF"]
			description: ["With Earth's noise blocked by 3,474 km of rock, the &6Deep Space Antenna&r hears a steady hiss from Sagittarius. You will go there. Mars first. Night on the Moon and your landing-site chart, which calibrates the dish. The Mars Transfer Chart, and with it the road to Mars. It runs unattended at night. Keep a data stick ready."]
			icon: "gtceu:deep_space_antenna"
			id: "5940CA99055BAF42"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "77023010782731C0", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ id: "1B174F9D773F1E2C", item: "gtceu:data_stick", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "1C33E0A1C8B74069", item: "gtceu:deep_space_antenna", type: "item" }]
			title: "Deep Space Antenna"
			x: 8.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1DC956E9F071636A"]
			description: [
				"The Earth-Moon bridge starts with a &6Lunar Quantum Seed&r, made in a chemical reactor up here from an ender pearl and helium-3. An ordinary singularity pair won't do: a lunar quantum chamber spits it out."
				"One half goes in a chamber at home, one here, and both ends stay chunk-loaded."
			]
			icon: "ae2:quantum_link"
			id: "366AB48E5BF50431"
			rewards: [{ id: "7E388C5B6B30F54B", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "76B12CF105EBB9FF", item: "grindless:lunar_quantum_seed", type: "item" }
				{ count: 2L, id: "7D3865E8AB3A4A6D", item: "ae2:quantum_entangled_singularity", type: "item" }
				{ count: 2L, id: "105F48A9288461CC", item: "ae2:quantum_link", type: "item" }
				{ count: 16L, id: "318D644FC6DE61F3", item: "ae2:quantum_ring", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Earth-Moon Bridge"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["366AB48E5BF50431"]
			description: [
				"Two &6EU P2P Tunnels&r on one frequency, one on a cable at home and one on a hatch up here, and the power plant on Earth runs the Moon."
				"The tunnels pass whatever voltage you feed them, so match it to the hatch at the far end. AE2 charges a small toll in AE energy for the delivery."
			]
			icon: "eup2p:eu_p2p_tunnel"
			id: "42BF2F77456F8773"
			rewards: [{ id: "5D6B28FB61E42CBD", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			tasks: [{ count: 2L, id: "751D67F4EBA6DE8C", item: "eup2p:eu_p2p_tunnel", type: "item" }]
			title: "Power from Earth"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["366AB48E5BF50431"]
			description: [
				"Once the first bridge is up, the Moon can make its own seeds in a chemical reactor up here, with ender pearls sent from home and helium-3 from the drill or the cell."
				"The seed travels home over the bridge, the explosion happens there, and one half travels back. Nobody has to fly."
			]
			icon: "grindless:lunar_quantum_seed"
			id: "38AA0491A1AFD8C9"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "5D23F1FDA315072E", type: "xp", xp: 50 }
				{ count: 4, id: "3CA3C104FB1DDB7B", item: "minecraft:ender_pearl", type: "item" }
			]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "11691B6B87A0E83E", item: "grindless:lunar_quantum_seed", type: "item" }
				{ count: 2L, id: "1BCF50880C918E54", item: "ae2:quantum_link", type: "item" }
				{ count: 16L, id: "172A4B25DF6871FF", item: "ae2:quantum_ring", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "A Second Pair, No Rocket"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5301384885D78BAC"]
			description: [
				"Blow the seed up with a singularity at home, then send one half to Mars. The Martian end needs no power of its own; once linked, it runs on the home network."
				"Chunk-load both ends, same as the Moon."
			]
			icon: "ae2:quantum_ring"
			id: "53893FAB153254B8"
			rewards: [{ id: "56844C1FA1C458D3", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
